[2026-05-23 12:35] HOTFIX-4 dispatch — layout nav still uses `$page.data?.session` (old BFF model). PO sees "Sign in" link even when signed in. Fix: derive `signedIn` from localStorage, reactive to navigation.

## Current bug

`src/routes/+layout.svelte`:
```svelte
const session = $derived($page.data?.session ?? null);
```

Under Path C, server load returns `{}`, so `session` is always null. Nav always shows "Sign in" link.

## Fix

Replace `$page.data.session` read with `getToken() !== null` check. Make it re-evaluate on navigation (layouts persist across SPA routes; can't rely on onMount alone).

### Updated `src/routes/+layout.svelte`

```svelte
<script lang="ts">
	import '../app.css';
	import { page } from '$app/stores';
	import { onMount } from 'svelte';
	import { getToken } from '$lib/auth/storage';
	import * as m from '$lib/paraglide/messages.js';

	let { children } = $props();

	let signedIn = $state(false);

	function refreshSignedIn() {
		signedIn = getToken() !== null;
	}

	onMount(() => {
		refreshSignedIn();

		// React to storage changes from other tabs (logout in one tab clears all)
		const onStorage = (e: StorageEvent) => {
			if (e.key === 'token' || e.key === null) refreshSignedIn();
		};
		window.addEventListener('storage', onStorage);
		return () => window.removeEventListener('storage', onStorage);
	});

	// Re-read on navigation (sign-in/out via internal goto won't fire storage event)
	$effect(() => {
		// Touch $page.url to make this $effect reactive to URL changes
		$page.url;
		refreshSignedIn();
	});
</script>

<header class="bg-white border-b border-gray-200 px-4 py-3">
	<nav class="max-w-5xl mx-auto flex items-center justify-between">
		<a href="/" class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900">mvox</a>
		<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
			{#if signedIn}
				<a href="/auth/logout" data-testid="nav-sign-out" class="text-sm text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900">
					{m.nav_sign_out()}
				</a>
			{:else}
				<a href="/auth/login" data-testid="nav-sign-in" class="text-sm text-gray-700 hover:text-gray-900">
					{m.nav_sign_in()}
				</a>
			{/if}
		</div>
	</nav>
</header>

<main class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 py-6">
	{@render children()}
</main>

<footer class="border-t border-gray-200 mt-8 px-4 py-4 text-center text-sm text-gray-500">
	mvox
</footer>
```

Note: `$page` is the legacy stores API; SvelteKit 2 still supports it. We're not moving to `$app/state` here — that's a separate cleanup. The pattern works fine.

Dropped: the `<span class="text-sm text-gray-600">{session.jwt ? '●' : ''}</span>` indicator dot. Could re-add later as a "user menu" trigger; for now, the sign-out link is enough.

## Scope confirmation

ONLY `src/routes/+layout.svelte`. No spec (no existing layout spec). E2E coverage is YELLOW-B.2 / CHORE-C scope.

