[2026-05-23 12:45] PRE-MERGE cleanup dispatch. One commit, two concerns: drop the dev scaffold + apply PO's "don't render auth controls before we know the state" principle.

## Concern 1: Drop `/dev/auth-controls` scaffold

```bash
rm -r src/routes/dev/
```

Net-zero in the squash; PO live-test is complete.

## Concern 2: Defer auth-state-dependent rendering until hydration

**Principle (PO directive):** "We shouldn't show any controls, ever, before we make sure that they make sense." SSR renders with `signedIn=false` default → user sees "Sign in" link briefly even when actually signed in. Same flash on landing page (signed-out CTA flashes before grid renders).

Fix: add a `mounted` flag, true only after onMount has read getToken(). Gate all auth-state-conditional rendering on `mounted`.

### `src/routes/+layout.svelte`

Add `mounted` state:
```svelte
let mounted = $state(false);
let signedIn = $state(false);

function refreshSignedIn() {
  signedIn = getToken() !== null;
}

onMount(() => {
  refreshSignedIn();
  mounted = true;
  // existing storage listener stays
  ...
});

// existing $effect stays
```

Template — wrap the auth controls in `{#if mounted}...{/if}`:
```svelte
<div class="flex items-center gap-4">
  {#if mounted}
    {#if signedIn}
      <a href="/auth/logout" data-testid="nav-sign-out" ...>{m.nav_sign_out()}</a>
    {:else}
      <a href="/auth/login" data-testid="nav-sign-in" ...>{m.nav_sign_in()}</a>
    {/if}
  {/if}
</div>
```

Empty `<div>` during SSR + first frame post-hydration, then the correct button appears once `mounted` flips. The brand link + footer + main content all render normally — only the auth controls are gated.

### `src/routes/+page.svelte` (landing)

Same pattern. Add `mounted = $state(false)`, set to true in onMount AFTER reading `signedIn`. Wrap the existing `{#if !signedIn}...{:else}...{/if}` block in `{#if mounted}...{/if}`.

```svelte
let mounted = $state(false);
let signedIn = $state(false);
// existing orgs / loadError / loaded state stays

onMount(() => {
  signedIn = getToken() !== null;
  mounted = true;
  if (signedIn) {
    fetchOrgs();
  }
});
```

Template — wrap top-level:
```svelte
{#if mounted}
  {#if !signedIn}
    <section class="py-16 text-center">
      ...signed-out CTA...
    </section>
  {:else}
    <section>
      ...signed-in org grid (existing template)...
    </section>
  {/if}
{/if}
```

During SSR + first frame: nothing renders in the auth-conditional area. After hydration: correct branch.

**Note on layout shift:** there will be a brief moment of empty space before content appears. Acceptable — better than flashing the wrong button. If we want to suppress shift entirely later, we can ship a skeleton; for now, the empty space is the right trade.

